# Riverpod

Riverpod is a reactive caching and data-binding framework for Dart and Flutter. It helps you fetch, cache and combine asynchronous data, handles loading and error states for you, and is compile-safe (no `ProviderNotFoundException`).

## Install

```bash
flutter pub add flutter_riverpod
```

```dart
final helloProvider = Provider((ref) => 'Hello world');

class Home extends ConsumerWidget {
  @override
  Widget build(BuildContext context, WidgetRef ref) => Text(ref.watch(helloProvider));
}
```

Wrap the app in `ProviderScope` to start using providers.

# React

React is a JavaScript library for building user interfaces. You describe the UI as a function of state with components, and React efficiently updates the DOM when the state changes.

## Install

```bash
npm install react react-dom
```

```jsx
function Counter() {
  const [count, setCount] = useState(0);
  return <button onClick={() => setCount(count + 1)}>Clicked {count} times</button>;
}
```

For a full app, start with a framework such as Next.js or React Router.

# Playwright

Playwright is a framework for web testing and automation. One API drives Chromium, Firefox and WebKit, with auto-waiting, tracing and parallel test execution.

## Get started

```bash
npm init playwright@latest
npx playwright test
```

```ts
import { test, expect } from '@playwright/test';

test('has title', async ({ page }) => {
  await page.goto('https://playwright.dev/');
  await expect(page).toHaveTitle(/Playwright/);
});
```
